msgstr "Setup {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import the libraries used throughout the tutorial and fix a random seed for reproducibility.\n"
msgstr "I-import ang mga library na ginagamit sa buong tutorial at magtakda ng random seed para sa reproducibility.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa sa maliit na sukat gamit ang simulator {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start with eight assets drawn from six sectors and select exactly $K=4$ of them. With only eight assets there are only $\\binom{8}{4}=70$ valid portfolios, so we can later check the quantum result against an exhaustive search.\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayo sa walong asset mula sa anim na sector at pipili ng eksaktong $K=4$ sa mga ito. Sa walong asset lang, mayroon lang $\\binom{8}{4}=70$ na valid na portfolio, kaya masusuri natin mamaya ang quantum na resulta laban sa exhaustive search.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga classical na input sa isang quantum na problema {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each asset is one qubit; a bitstring like `10110010` is a portfolio (the 1s are the assets we hold). We need three ingredients: the market data, the three objective Hamiltonians, and a circuit that only ever proposes portfolios with exactly $K$ assets.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat asset ay isang qubit; ang bitstring na gaya ng `10110010` ay isang portfolio (ang mga 1 ay ang mga asset na hawak natin). Kailangan natin ng tatlong sangkap: ang market data, ang tatlong objective Hamiltonian, at isang circuit na nagmumungkahi lang ng mga portfolio na may eksaktong $K$ asset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Enforcing \"exactly K assets\" without a penalty.** A common trick is to add a penalty term that punishes portfolios of the wrong size, but that couples every qubit to every other qubit, which leads to much deeper circuits after transpilation. Instead we use an **XY mixer**, which only ever moves the QAOA state *between* bitstrings of the same Hamming weight. If we start in a state that already has $K$ assets selected, every portfolio the circuit explores also has exactly $K$ assets. The constraint is built into the circuit's structure rather than enforced by a penalty term.\n"
msgstr "**Pagpapatupad ng \"eksaktong K asset\" nang walang penalty.** Karaniwang paraan ang magdagdag ng penalty term na pumaparusa sa mga portfolio na mali ang laki, ngunit iniuugnay nito ang bawat qubit sa bawat isa pang qubit, na humahantong sa mas malalalim na circuit pagkatapos ng transpilation. Sa halip, gumagamit tayo ng **XY mixer**, na naglilipat lang sa QAOA state *sa pagitan* ng mga bitstring na may parehong Hamming weight. Kung magsisimula tayo sa state na mayroon nang $K$ napiling asset, ang bawat portfolio na sinusuri ng circuit ay mayroon ding eksaktong $K$ asset. Ang constraint ay nakapaloob sa estruktura ng circuit sa halip na ipinapatupad ng penalty term.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the starting state cheaply: rotate each qubit so it is \"on\" with probability $K/N$. Restricted to the $K$-asset outcomes, this reproduces the ideal equal-weight (Dicke) state, so we simply keep the measured bitstrings that have exactly $K$ ones — a step called *post-selection*.\n"
msgstr "Inihahanda natin nang mura ang panimulang state: i-rotate ang bawat qubit para ito ay \"on\" na may probability na $K/N$. Kapag nilimitahan sa mga outcome na may $K$ asset, nirereproduce nito ang ideal na equal-weight (Dicke) state, kaya itinatago na lang natin ang mga nasukat na bitstring na may eksaktong $K$ na 1 — isang hakbang na tinatawag na *post-selection*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before running, the abstract circuit is transpiled into hardware-native gates. At this small scale we only inspect the cost: how deep is the circuit and how many two-qubit gates does it use? (Two-qubit gates are the main source of noise on real devices.)\n"
msgstr "Bago patakbuhin, ang abstract na circuit ay tina-transpile sa mga hardware-native na gate. Sa maliit na sukat na ito, sinisilip lang natin ang gastos: gaano kalalim ang circuit at ilang two-qubit gate ang ginagamit nito? (Ang mga two-qubit gate ang pangunahing pinagmumulan ng noise sa mga totoong device.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Patakbuhin gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two stages. First we **train** the QAOA angles once, using equal objective weights, with an exact statevector simulator to find good $\\beta,\\gamma$ values. Then we **sweep** many weight vectors across the simplex and sample the circuit at each, collecting candidate portfolios. Because only the objective weights change between sweeps (not the trained angles), all the weight vectors are submitted in a single batched job.\n"
msgstr "Dalawang yugto. Una, **sinasanay** natin ang mga QAOA angle nang isang beses, gamit ang pantay na objective weight, sa isang exact statevector simulator para mahanap ang magagandang halaga ng $\\beta,\\gamma$. Pagkatapos, **iniikot** natin ang maraming weight vector sa simplex at sina-sample ang circuit sa bawat isa, na nangongolekta ng mga kandidatong portfolio. Dahil ang mga objective weight lang ang nagbabago sa pagitan ng mga sweep (hindi ang mga sinanay na angle), lahat ng weight vector ay isinusumite sa iisang batched na job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We keep only the feasible portfolios (exactly $K$ assets from the post-selection step), score each one on all three objectives, and extract the **Pareto front**: the portfolios that are not beaten on every objective at once. The *hypervolume* is a single number summarizing how much objective space the front dominates, and bigger is better.\n"
msgstr "Itinatago lang natin ang mga feasible na portfolio (eksaktong $K$ asset mula sa post-selection step), binibigyan ng score ang bawat isa sa lahat ng tatlong layunin, at kinukuha ang **Pareto front**: ang mga portfolio na hindi natatalo sa lahat ng layunin nang sabay. Ang *hypervolume* ay isang numerong nagbubuod kung gaano karaming objective space ang dinodomina ng front, at mas malaki ay mas mabuti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With 100,000 shots over only 256 bitstrings, this run sees every one of the 70 valid portfolios, so at this size it is effectively a brute-force check that the pipeline is wired correctly, rather than evidence that QAOA found the front.\n"
msgstr "Sa 100,000 shot sa 256 na bitstring lang, nakikita ng run na ito ang bawat isa sa 70 valid na portfolio, kaya sa laking ito ay isa itong epektibong brute-force na pagsusuri na tama ang pagkakakabit ng pipeline, at hindi ebidensya na nahanap ng QAOA ang front.\n"

