msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-approximate-multi-objective-optimization/extracted-outputs/9ccde65a-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa sa hardware sa malaking sukat {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the same workflow on **40 assets** (8 sectors × 5), choosing $K=6$. Forty qubits is too large to simulate exactly (a $2^{40}$-amplitude statevector), so the angles can't be optimized the way they were at eight assets, and a dense circuit would be too deep for current hardware. The $\\binom{40}{6} \\approx 3.8$M valid portfolios are still few enough to enumerate classically, which we use at the end as an exact benchmark. Several things change, and **nothing else about the method does**:\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay ang parehong workflow sa **40 asset** (8 sector × 5), na pumipili ng $K=6$. Ang apatnapung qubit ay masyadong malaki para i-simulate nang eksakto (isang statevector na may $2^{40}$ amplitude), kaya hindi maaaring i-optimize ang mga angle gaya ng ginawa sa walong asset, at ang isang dense na circuit ay masyadong malalim para sa kasalukuyang hardware. Ang $\\binom{40}{6} \\approx 3.8$M na valid na portfolio ay sapat pa ring kaunti para bilangin nang classical, na ginagamit natin sa dulo bilang exact na benchmark. Maraming bagay ang nagbabago, at **walang iba pang nagbabago sa pamamaraan**:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Train the angles with a matrix-product-state (MPS) simulator, not exact statevector.** Following the reference (Kotil et al.), we fix the objective weights to equal values, optimize a single β, γ on the MPS simulator, and reuse them for every weighting vector in the sweep. (We train at the size we run — no small-to-large angle transfer.)\n"
msgstr "**Sanayin ang mga angle gamit ang matrix-product-state (MPS) simulator, hindi exact statevector.** Alinsunod sa reference (Kotil et al.), itinatakda natin ang mga objective weight sa pantay na halaga, ino-optimize ang iisang β, γ sa MPS simulator, at ginagamit muli ang mga ito sa bawat weighting vector sa sweep. (Sinasanay natin sa laking pinapatakbo natin — walang small-to-large na angle transfer.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sparsify the risk model to fit hardware.** A full covariance couples all 780 asset pairs. We keep only the strongest, cheapest-to-route couplings using *importance-aware QAP truncation*, and couple each sector in a light ring for the diversity term. This keeps the objectives meaningful while holding the circuit to a hardware-friendly size.\n"
msgstr "**I-sparsify ang risk model para magkasya sa hardware.** Ang buong covariance ay nag-uugnay sa lahat ng 780 pares ng asset. Itinatago lang natin ang pinakamalalakas at pinakamurang i-route na mga coupling gamit ang *importance-aware QAP truncation*, at iniuugnay ang bawat sector sa isang magaan na ring para sa diversity term. Pinananatili nitong makabuluhan ang mga layunin habang hawak ang circuit sa laking angkop sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Keep the circuit shallow and score honestly.** Routing is stochastic, so we transpile with several seeds and keep the shallowest (and no quantum time is spent). Portfolios are always **scored against the true, full objectives**. The sparsification only shapes the circuit, not how portfolios are judged.\n"
msgstr "**Panatilihing mababaw ang circuit at magbigay ng tapat na score.** Stochastic ang routing, kaya nagta-transpile tayo gamit ang ilang seed at itinatago ang pinakamababaw (at walang quantum time na nauubos). Ang mga portfolio ay palaging **sinusukat laban sa totoo at buong mga layunin**. Ang sparsification ay humuhubog lang sa circuit, hindi sa paraan ng paghusga sa mga portfolio.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Why QAP truncation?\">\n"
"Keeping each asset's largest couplings by magnitude alone can result in a circuit that is sparse but still awkward to route. QAP truncation instead keeps couplings that are both large *and* physically close on the chip, so the same gate budget buys a shallower, more hardware-friendly circuit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Bakit QAP truncation?\">\n"
"Ang pagtatago lang ng pinakamalalaking coupling ng bawat asset batay sa magnitude ay maaaring magresulta sa circuit na sparse ngunit mahirap pa ring i-route. Sa halip, itinatago ng QAP truncation ang mga coupling na parehong malaki *at* pisikal na malapit sa chip, kaya ang parehong gate budget ay nagbibigay ng mas mababaw at mas hardware-friendly na circuit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map inputs (sparsified for hardware) {#step-1-map-inputs-sparsified-for-hardware}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga input (na-sparsify para sa hardware) {#step-1-map-inputs-sparsified-for-hardware}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 2-3: train the angles, then build and submit the hardware job {#steps-2-3-train-the-angles-then-build-and-submit-the-hardware-job}"
msgstr "Mga Hakbang 2-3: sanayin ang mga angle, pagkatapos ay buuin at isumite ang hardware job {#steps-2-3-train-the-angles-then-build-and-submit-the-hardware-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Forty qubits is too large to optimize the angles exactly, so we train one $\\beta, \\gamma$ on a\n"
"matrix-product-state simulator at equal objective weights and reuse them across the sweep.\n"
"The cell below loads pre-trained values from a file. The trained cost-layer angle is small\n"
"($\\gamma \\approx 0.32$), so the circuit applies a gentle bias rather than a sharp projection.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang apatnapung qubit ay masyadong malaki para i-optimize nang eksakto ang mga angle, kaya sinasanay natin ang iisang $\\beta, \\gamma$ sa isang\n"
"matrix-product-state simulator sa pantay na objective weight at ginagamit muli ang mga ito sa buong sweep.\n"
"Ang cell sa ibaba ay naglo-load ng mga pre-trained na halaga mula sa isang file. Maliit ang sinanay na cost-layer angle\n"
"($\\gamma \\approx 0.32$), kaya ang circuit ay naglalapat ng banayad na bias sa halip na matalas na projection.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process into the Pareto front and read off the optimal portfolios {#step-4-post-process-into-the-pareto-front-and-read-off-the-optimal-portfolios}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process tungo sa Pareto front at basahin ang mga optimal na portfolio {#step-4-post-process-into-the-pareto-front-and-read-off-the-optimal-portfolios}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this problem size, QAOA performs about as well as uniform random sampling. Both recover a large fraction of the exact optimum's hypervolume, and neither is clearly ahead. This outcome is expected for a single shallow QAOA layer with a heavily truncated cost operator on noisy hardware; the value of this example is the end-to-end multi-objective workflow (mapping, angle training, constrained sampling, and Pareto post-processing), not a quantum speed-up. Narrowing the gap to the optimum would call for deeper circuits (more QAOA layers), a gentler truncation, or lower-noise hardware.\n"
msgstr "Sa laking ito ng problema, halos kasing-husay ng uniform random sampling ang QAOA. Pareho silang nakakabawi ng malaking bahagi ng hypervolume ng exact na optimum, at walang malinaw na nangunguna. Inaasahan ang resultang ito para sa isang mababaw na QAOA layer na may lubhang pinutol na cost operator sa maingay na hardware; ang halaga ng halimbawang ito ay ang end-to-end na multi-objective workflow (mapping, angle training, constrained sampling, at Pareto post-processing), hindi ang quantum speed-up. Ang pagpapaliit ng agwat sa optimum ay mangangailangan ng mas malalalim na circuit (mas maraming QAOA layer), mas banayad na truncation, o hardware na mas mababa ang noise.\n"

